Data-source attributions and terms:

- The Elliptic dataset (Weber et al., "Anti-Money Laundering in Bitcoin:
  Experimenting with Graph Convolutional Networks for Financial Forensics",
  arXiv:1908.02591, 2019) is used by the legacy benchmark path. It is
  downloaded at run time (`openheads.download_elliptic`) from its public
  distribution and is NOT redistributed in this repository. Use of the
  dataset is subject to its own terms.
- The label-set builder (`scripts/build_label_set.py`) queries public label
  sources you configure at run time (public designation lists and public
  attribution repositories). No third-party label data ships in this
  repository.

This repository ships NO datasets, NO assembled label set, NO graph
substrate or embeddings, NO threshold values, and NO trained model weights
(see README "Boundary"). Training inputs are parameters the user supplies;
warehouse configuration is fail-closed, with no default storage location
anywhere in the tree.

Outputs derived from CC-BY-NC sources (e.g. OpenSanctions) or BSL-licensed
sources (e.g. Dune Spellbook) must not be added to this repository.
